  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.94,
      "end_seconds": 7.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "doctor, hi, where would you like me to put my coat?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.52,
      "end_seconds": 13.58,
      "duration_seconds": 5.06,
      "text": "Yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.66,
      "end_seconds": 18.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I'm here because of my heart suddenly racing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.11,
      "end_seconds": 23.42,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.33,
      "end_seconds": 27.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "It started yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 28.69,
      "end_seconds": 32.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Have you been feeling lightheaded during an episode?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.13,
      "end_seconds": 53.28,
      "duration_seconds": 19.15,
      "text": "well, yes, for three weeks. Okay, you know, so as for feeling lightheaded during an episode, it feels moderate to me. Actually, I did have a pounding in my neck at one point, but that's gone now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.26,
      "end_seconds": 61.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "And what about family history of sudden death, breathlessness, fainting or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.8,
      "end_seconds": 69.44,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "No, no family history of sudden death, breathlessness, fainting or chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.97,
      "end_seconds": 73.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.79,
      "end_seconds": 76.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.31,
      "end_seconds": 82.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 84.82,
      "end_seconds": 94.92,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "Asthma, for five years my sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.7,
      "end_seconds": 100.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "yes, asthma is known to us, good to have that clear"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.59,
      "end_seconds": 117.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.26,
      "end_seconds": 137.53,
      "duration_seconds": 19.27,
      "text": "yes, I had my appendix taken out, when I was in my twenties i wasn't sure whether to to come in at all, to be honest i looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.34,
      "end_seconds": 141.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "A few questions about your lifestyle now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.59,
      "end_seconds": 160.04,
      "duration_seconds": 16.45,
      "text": "Nothing, I'm teetotal. I have about eight cigarettes in a day. Yes, I work in a bakery, early starts. I live with my elderly mother. I swim twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.42,
      "end_seconds": 164.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "what do you take on a normal day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.91,
      "end_seconds": 171.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Seretide inhaler, twice a day for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.81,
      "end_seconds": 188.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "let's start with the basic checks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.04,
      "end_seconds": 198.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Sit still for a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.11,
      "end_seconds": 223.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.38,
      "text": "Okay: pulse 73, temperature is 36.9 degrees, BP is 117 over 72."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 224.68,
      "end_seconds": 226.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 228.24,
      "end_seconds": 230.69,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "We'll go over that shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.68,
      "end_seconds": 235.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "May I examine you now?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.38,
      "end_seconds": 238.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 246.44,
      "end_seconds": 250.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Your heart sounds and rhythm are normal today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.88,
      "end_seconds": 252.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "okay, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.05,
      "end_seconds": 267.5,
      "duration_seconds": 12.45,
      "text": "Okay, that's all I needed to check. From what you've told me and what I found, it points towards episodes of supraventricular tachycardia. Atrial fibrillation is still possible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.41,
      "end_seconds": 272.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "is there something to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 274.58,
      "end_seconds": 282.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with episodes of supraventricular tachycardia do well once it's treated properly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 298.37,
      "end_seconds": 329.46,
      "duration_seconds": 31.09,
      "text": "I'll request a thyroid test, it'll help with palpitations. A 7-day heart monitor is what I'd like next, for paroxysmal palpitations. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. An ECG is what I'd like next, for palpitations. Try blowing hard against a closed mouth and nose when it starts. I think the cardiology clinic should see you too. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 330.41,
      "end_seconds": 333.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Uh, thank you, that's helpful."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.44,
      "end_seconds": 337.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "So, all the best."
    }
  ]
}